If you can do both Wizard and Valkyrie, you can do Tourist.  The early
game (which is undeniably the hard part) plays mostly like for
Wizards,
except that you start out with a helpful stack of +2 darts (which is
useful for surviving until you find some daggers) and an unlocking
device, instead of the spellbook of force bolt.  The late game can be
played mostly like a Valkyrie except that you get much better spell
rates and can recharge wands and tools entirely for free, which is
awesome.  The middle game is distinctive mainly in terms of the
impressive amount of loot you get from the quest, more than for any
other role I've played.  You can use pretty much any weapon you want,
and by mid-game you can cast mid-level spells.

